  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Batoka Dairy Cooperative Society Milk Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Agriculture (dairy), Beneficiaries: 140 small-scale dairy farmers, Location: It is situated in Choma District, Southern province. , Summary: BDCS lacked management and operational capacity to run the enterprise as a profitable and sustainable operation and did not have a management team to oversee operations. Milk production from individual beef cows was low at 1 liter per cow per day resulting in members getting limited income, and their existing chilling tank had a capacity of only 1,500 liters and was filled within a day leaving significant quantities of milk going to waste. The support from USADF will allow BDCS to address these constraints including almost doubling their storage capacity and introducing an AI program.</narrative>
  </description>
